# HumSukhan Environment Configuration
#
# This file documents the build-time variables consumed by the app.
#
# ─── How to supply values ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Option A: --dart-define (single values)
#
#   flutter run \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGci...
#
# Option B: --dart-define-from-file (all values from a file)
#
#   1. Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
#   2. Run:  flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
#
# ⚠  .env is gitignored — never commit real keys.
# ⚠  Only use the Supabase PUBLISHABLE (anon) key.
#    Never use the service_role or sb_secret key in the client.
#
# ─── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL           – Project URL from Supabase dashboard.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY      – Publishable (anon) key. NOT the service_role key.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key-here

# ─── Google Gemini API ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The GEMINI_API_KEY is no longer supplied to the Flutter client.
# It is stored as a Supabase server-side secret and used only by the
# generate-insights Edge Function.
#
# Deploy steps:
#   supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=<your-gemini-api-key>
#   supabase functions deploy generate-insights
